  "body": "What happens: the Sinumerik 840D post writes `T<n> D<n> M6`, so tool 12 gets `D12`. With the default tool management, D selects a cutting edge of the active tool (1-9). A high tool number then gives an alarm, or selects an empty edge with no length.\n\nExpected: write `D1` by default. Let the machine file state another rule (for example \"D equals T\" for a control set to flat D numbers).\n\nEvidence: `assets/posts/sinumerik.cps:505` on upstream/main `f0bdc5109`.\n\nFound by the post audit against the SINUMERIK manuals (#4130).\n\nDone means: the default output is `T<n> D1 M6`. A machine-file setting selects another D rule. A test pins both.\n",
